# Forge — per-machine engine settings.
#
# Copy to ~/.config/forge/forge.env and edit. That path is per-machine on
# purpose: the same vault checkout is a GPU box on one machine and a laptop
# borrowing a hosted endpoint on another, and the vault is shared by Git.
#
#     mkdir -p ~/.config/forge
#     cp config/forge.env.example ~/.config/forge/forge.env
#     chmod 600 ~/.config/forge/forge.env      # it can hold an API key
#
# Format: KEY=value, one per line. `#` comments, blank lines, a leading
# `export `, and surrounding quotes are all fine. No interpolation, no command
# substitution — a settings file that can execute is one that can surprise you.
#
# The process environment always wins, so any line here can be overridden for a
# single command:  FORGE_LLM_PROVIDER=mock forge status
#
# Check what got loaded with:  forge status
# Full reference:              docs/cli.md

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Profile A — the GPU box (Ollama). This is the whole file on that machine.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

FORGE_MODEL_DEFAULT=qwen3:8b
FORGE_LLM_TIMEOUT=600

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Profile B — a laptop driving the GPU box over a private network.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Reaches Ollama on another host; nothing assumes the model is local. Use a
# Tailscale/WireGuard hostname rather than a public address — Ollama has no
# authentication, so anything that can reach port 11434 can use it.
#
# FORGE_OLLAMA_URL=http://asus:11434
# FORGE_MODEL_DEFAULT=qwen3:8b
# FORGE_LLM_TIMEOUT=600

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Profile C — a laptop on a hosted open-weights endpoint, for when the GPU box
# is off. No paid API is required anywhere in Forge; this is one option.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# A preset fills in the endpoint, the credential variable name, and a sane
# token ceiling. You still choose the model — that is never guessed for you.
# Presets: groq, openrouter, together, cerebras, fireworks, lmstudio,
# llama-cpp, vllm. Any other OpenAI-compatible host works without one; set
# FORGE_CLOUD_VENDOR=openai and FORGE_CLOUD_BASE_URL yourself.
#
# FORGE_LLM_PROVIDER=cloud
# FORGE_CLOUD_PRESET=groq
# FORGE_CLOUD_MODEL=llama-3.3-70b-versatile
# GROQ_API_KEY=gsk_...
# FORGE_LLM_TIMEOUT=600

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Notes
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# * The key is read at call time and never written to config, the derived
#   store, provenance, or logs — and never copied into the environment.
#   `forge status` reports whether one is present without echoing it.
# * Open-weights models cap output well below a frontier model. A preset picks
#   a safe ceiling; override with FORGE_CLOUD_MAX_TOKENS if the host rejects it.
# * A measured quality result belongs to a *model*, not to Forge. Changing
#   provider or model means re-running the evaluation, not inheriting the old
#   number — see docs/cli.md, "Re-measure after any provider change".
